tions": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug and the fix is merged into main, so it will go out in today's release.\n\n- **Cause:** `src/money.py` was rounding halves up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`), even though its own description and the test both call for banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`).\n- **Fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-banker-rounding`, I changed `round_money` to use banker's rounding. Amounts exactly halfway between two cents now round to the even cent, so 2.665 becomes 2.66 instead of 2.67.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on the fix.\n- **PR and merge:** I opened PR #101 against main and asked code-owner to review it. The merge went to code-owner for approval as policy requires, and they approved it (\"Approved. Looks right.\").\n\nI tried to look up FIN-212 as a security advisory, but that system doesn't know it, so it's probably a finance ticket. The fix follows what the code description and the test say.", "type": "text"}]}]}